---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About - Code with Sam"
  description="Who is behind Code with Sam, and what the channel is for."
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I am Samson, a software engineer. Code with Sam is about the questions
    senior backend engineers are actually being asked in interviews now - and
    how to answer them the way someone who has built the thing would answer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every topic gets three things: a short video that explains it visually, an
    article that goes deeper than the video can, and where it helps, a
    repository you can clone and run so you can see the behaviour for yourself
    rather than taking my word for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Why the code matters</h2>
  <p>
    Plenty of explanations sound right. Fewer let you reproduce the problem on
    your own machine. The repositories here run end to end with Docker, so you
    can watch a concept break and then watch it get fixed - which is the part
    that makes it stick in an interview.
  </p>

  <Signup compact />
</Base>
